job-description-sitedirector = The Site Director manages the other Command Staff, and through them the rest of the facility. Though they have access to everything, they do not understand everything, and are expected to delegate tasks to the appropriate crew member. The Site Director is expected to have an understanding of Standard Operating Procedure, and is subject to it, and legal action, in the same way as every other crew member.
job-outpost-description-hop = The Head of Personnel manages the Service department and most other civilians. They also manage the Supply department, through the Quartermaster. In addition, the Head of Personnel oversees the personal accounts of the crew, including their money and access. If necessary, the Head of Personnel is first in line to assume Acting Command.
job-outpost-description-qm = The Quartermaster manages the Supply department, checking cargo orders and ensuring supplies get to where they are needed.
job-outpost-description-cargotech = A Cargo Technician fills and delivers cargo orders.
job-outpost-description-shaftminer = A Shaft Miner mines and processes minerals to be delivered to departments that need them.
job-outpost-description-hos = The Head of Security manages the Security Department, keeping the facility safe and making sure the rules are followed. They are expected to keep the other Department Heads, and the rest of the crew, aware of developing situations that may be a threat. If necessary, the HoS may perform the duties of absent Security roles, such as distributing gear from the Armory.
job-outpost-description-warden = The Warden watches over the physical Security Department, making sure the Brig and Armoury are secure and in order at all times. They oversee prisoners that have been processed and brigged, and are responsible for their well being. The Warden is also in charge of distributing Armoury gear in a crisis, and retrieving it when the crisis has passed. In an emergency, the Warden may be called upon to direct the Security Department as a whole.
job-outpost-description-security = A Security Officer is concerned with maintaining the safety and security of the facility as a whole, dealing with external threats and apprehending criminals. A Security Officer is responsible for the health, safety, and processing of any prisoner they arrest. No one is above the Law, not Security or Command.
job-outpost-description-stowaway = Escaped clone, social outcast, ex-employee, or sentient wildlife; The maintenance tunnels of the facility are your home. While you have no real authority or responsibility, your survival requires you to cooperate with the crew. This is not an antag role, but you may still defend yourself.
job-outpost-description-bartender = A Bartender mixes drinks for the crew. They generally have permission to charge for drinks or deny service to unruly patrons.
job-outpost-description-chaplain = The Chaplain ministers to the spiritual needs of the crew.
job-outpost-description-chef = A Chef cooks food for the crew. They generally have permission to charge for food or deny service to unruly diners.
job-outpost-description-botanist = A Botanist grows plants for the Chef and Bartender.
job-outpost-description-janitor = A Janitor keeps the facility clean, as long as it doesn't interfere with active crime scenes.
job-outpost-description-librarian = The Librarian curates the book selection in the Library, so the crew might enjoy it.
job-outpost-description-iaa = An Internal Affairs Agent makes sure that the crew is following Standard Operating Procedure. They also handle complaints against crew members, and can have issues brought to the attention of Corporate, assuming their paperwork is in order.
job-outpost-description-radiohost = A Radio Host's job includes playing music, singing songs, tell stories, or reading your favorite fanfic. You are the radiowave gremlin of the facility make sure everyone else knows that!
job-outpost-description-ce = The Chief Engineer manages the Engineering Department, ensuring that the Engineers work on what needs to be done, handling distribution of manpower as much as they handle hands-on operations and repairs. They are also expected to keep the rest of the facility informed of any structural threats to the facility that may be hazardous to health or disruptive to work.
job-outpost-description-engineer = An Engineer keeps the facility running. They repair damages, keep the atmosphere stable, and ensure that power is being generated and distributed. On quiet shifts, they may be called upon to make cosmetic alterations to the facility.
job-outpost-description-roboticist = A Roboticist maintains and repairs the facility synthetics, including crew with prosthetic limbs. They can also assist the facility by producing simple robots and even pilotable exosuits.
job-outpost-description-rd = The Research Director manages and maintains the R&D department. They are required to ensure the safety of the entire crew, at least with regards to anything occurring in the R&D department, and to inform the crew of any disruptions that might originate from R&D. The Research Director often has at least passing knowledge of most of the Research department, but are encouraged to allow their staff to perform their own duties.
job-outpost-description-scientist = A Scientist is a generalist working in the R&D department, with general knowledge of the scientific process, as well as the principles and requirements of Research and Development. They may also formulate experiments of their own devising, if they find an appropriate topic.
job-outpost-description-cmo = The CMO manages the Medical department and is a position requiring experience and skill; their goal is to ensure that their staff keep the facility's crew healthy and whole. They are primarily interested in making sure that patients are safely found and transported to Medical for treatment. They are expected to keep the crew informed about threats to their health and safety, and about the importance of Suit Sensors.
job-outpost-description-chemist = A Chemist produces and maintains a stock of basic to advanced chemicals for medical and occasionally research use. They are likely to know the use and dangers of many lab-produced chemicals.
job-outpost-description-doctor = A Doctor is a Jack-of-All-Trades Medical title, covering a variety of skill levels and minor specializations. They are likely familiar with basic first aid, and a number of accompanying medications, and can generally save, if not cure, a majority of the patients they encounter.
job-outpost-description-paramedic = A Chemist produces and maintains a stock of basic to advanced chemicals for medical and occasionally research use. They are likely to know the use and dangers of many lab-produced chemicals.
job-outpost-description-psychiatrist = A Psychiatrist provides mental health services to crew members in need. They may also be called upon to determine whatever ails the mentally unwell, frequently under Security supervision. They understand the effects of various psychoactive drugs.
job-outpost-description-ai = The AI oversees the operation of the facility and its crew, but has no real authority over them. The AI is required to follow its Laws, and Lawbound Synthetics that are linked to it are expected to follow the AI's commands, and their own Laws.
job-outpost-description-borg = A Cyborg is a mobile facility synthetic, piloted by a cybernetically preserved brain. It is considered a person, but is still required to follow its Laws.
job-outpost-description-xenobiologist = A Xenobiologist studies esoteric lifeforms, usually in the relative safety of their lab. They attempt to find ways to benefit from the byproducts of these lifeforms, and their main subject at present is the Giant Slime.
job-outpost-description-clown = A Clown is there to entertain the crew and keep high morale using various harmless pranks and ridiculous jokes!
job-outpost-description-mime = A Mime is there to entertain the crew and keep high morale using unbelievable performances and acting skills!
job-outpost-description-explorer = An Explorer searches for interesting things, and returns them to the facility.
